# Ignore rules for `docker build -f apps/server/Dockerfile .`
#
# The name matters. Docker reads `.dockerignore` from the root of the build
# context, and this image is built from the monorepo root — so a file at
# apps/server/.dockerignore would be silently ignored. BuildKit (default since
# Docker 23, and what Coolify uses) looks for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore`
# first, which is what lets each app have its own list.

# --- never ------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
**/node_modules
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# The generated Prisma client. It is rebuilt inside the image by
# `pnpm --filter @contextjule/db db:generate`, and a host-built copy carries
# the host's platform binaries — which on a Windows or macOS machine are the
# wrong ones for this Debian image.
packages/db/prisma/generated

# Secrets. Every one of them is injected at container start; none is needed at
# build time. A stray .env in the context is one COPY away from being baked
# into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- not part of this image -------------------------------------------------
# The Tauri app. src-tauri/target alone is gigabytes of Rust build output.
apps/desktop
# The marketing site. Its own image builds from apps/web/Dockerfile.
apps/web
# React components, fonts and the sprite engine — nothing the API imports.
packages/ui

# The design archive: ~100 PNGs and four multi-hundred-kilobyte HTML sheets.
designs
docs
scripts

# --- noise ------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
README.md
AGENTS.md
docker-compose.yml
biome.json
bts.jsonc
